WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.220
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson has promised "the&nbsp;
hierarchy of power is about to change" in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.480
DCEU. But who exactly is Black Adam,&nbsp;
and how does he fit into the series'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.432
timeline? Here's everything we know about&nbsp;
this anti-hero's history – and his future.

00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:15.971
Warning, spoilers ahead.

00:00:16.054 --> 00:00:16.998
"Here we go."

00:00:16.998 --> 00:00:22.980
Possibly the oldest DCEU character&nbsp;
to date, Black Adam was born five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.540
thousand years ago, likely predating even&nbsp;
Wonder Woman's birth. Teth-Adam began as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:32.280
slave of the fictional country Kahndaq where&nbsp;
he lost his son, who died saving his father.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:38.100
In the comics, the wizard Shazam grants Teth-Adam&nbsp;
the powers of gods, not knowing that the former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.620
slave holds no restraint in delivering deadly&nbsp;
justice to his abusers. In Black Adam's original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.660
comic book origin from Fawcett Comics, which takes&nbsp;
place before the character was acquired by DC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:53.340
he destroys the Pharaoh and Kahndaq's elite&nbsp;
before claiming the throne for himself.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.500
After Black Adam's rampage in Kahndaq,&nbsp;
the wizard realizes his mistake in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.520
bestowing Teth-Adam with the powers&nbsp;
of gods. Unable to remove his powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:08.580
Shazam renames the violent being "Black Adam"&nbsp;
and banishes him from the world of mankind.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:13.200
In the original Fawcett origin, the wizard&nbsp;
teleports Black Adam to the other side of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:19.200
the universe, forcing the villain to spend the&nbsp;
next 5,000 years flying back to Earth. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.000
the film's teaser shows the wizard Shazam&nbsp;
using his magic to seemingly entomb Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.500
Adam for thousands of years, giving him time&nbsp;
to find a new champion. In the modern day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.580
humans free the demigod, who&nbsp;
awakens in a strange new world.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.980
By the time Black Adam escapes his&nbsp;
tomb, the citizens of the DCEU have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.820
already experienced plenty of&nbsp;
bizarre and dangerous threats.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:47.160
Aliens from Krypton tried to destroy the world.&nbsp;
A beast known as Doomsday nearly destroyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.440
Metropolis and killed Superman. Atlantean armies&nbsp;
fought over whether or not to destroy life on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.600
the surface world. The Enchantress nearly&nbsp;
toppled Midway City. A giant starfish named&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.000
Starro visited terror upon Corto Maltese. And&nbsp;
alien butterflies threatened to take over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.980
world. Thankfully, humanity lives in an era&nbsp;
of superheroes who can combat such threats.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:13.620
HBO Max's "Peacemaker" series offers a&nbsp;
clue as to when Black Adam emerges into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:18.900
this age of heroes. In the fourth episode the&nbsp;
anti-hero Vigilante gets himself arrested to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.980
get thrown into prison and kill Peacemaker's&nbsp;
father. In a courtyard where security guards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.060
are having lunch, one guard is seen reading&nbsp;
a newspaper with an article indicating an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.840
organization known as "Intergang'' has&nbsp;
seized power in the nation of Kahndaq.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:35.460
In DC Comics, Intergang is a criminal&nbsp;
organization that uses advanced weaponry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.840
obtained from the alien planet Apokolips&nbsp;
to further their agenda. Since Black Adam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.760
considers himself the protector of Kahndaq, once&nbsp;
he returns, he'll definitely want to have a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.680
words with Intergang. This suggests "Black&nbsp;
Adam" will occur sometime after "Peacemaker."

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.580
In comic book lore, there have&nbsp;
been several versions of Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.980
Adam and his origins. In "Shazam! Vol. 1,"&nbsp;
written by DC comics maestro Geoff Johns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.960
we learn Black Adam is imprisoned by the wizard in&nbsp;
a tomb for his evil deeds, much like in the movie.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.460
While researching the villain, Shazam's current&nbsp;
champion Billy Batson gets a glimpse into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:13.320
past and witnesses a boy named Aman trying to&nbsp;
survive oppression along with his uncle. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:18.060
boy is given powers by the wizard Shazam,&nbsp;
and Billy incorrectly assumes Aman becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:22.440
Black Adam. However, he later learns&nbsp;
Aman's uncle steals his nephew's power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:26.700
kills The Wizard's intended champion,&nbsp;
and transforms into Black Adam.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.380
In the modern age, Dr. Sivana uncovers the&nbsp;
entrance to Black Adam's prison. He says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.140
the magic word, "Shazam!" and frees Black Adam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:39.360
who goes in search of Billy Batson in an attempt&nbsp;
to defeat him and become the ultimate champion.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.920
The new DCEU film makes changes to&nbsp;
the comic book origin, focusing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.180
Teth-Adam's relationship with his son,&nbsp;
not his nephew. The movie also doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.220
feature Shazam or his young counterpart Billy&nbsp;
Batson. However, Black Adam does get released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:58.380
from his magical prison to bring his brand of&nbsp;
justice down on those he deems deserving of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.840
his rage. This puts him in conflict with many&nbsp;
of Earth's heroes, including some new faces.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:10.680
Black Adam's primary antagonists will be the&nbsp;
Justice Society of America. The JSA is a group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:16.860
of heroes who came together during DC's Golden Age&nbsp;
of comics in the 1940s. In many DC continuities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:21.540
the JSA predates the Justice League and&nbsp;
clashed with the enemies of its era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:26.880
including the tyrannical Nazi regime. While&nbsp;
JSA members have all appeared in modern comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:33.580
the JSA is typically recognized as a superhero&nbsp;
team from a classic era with much older heroes.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.932
"The only thing we can learn from these&nbsp;
geezers is how to add more fiber to our diets!"

00:04:37.932 --> 00:04:42.600
The JSA includes famous members such&nbsp;
as the original Flash, Jay Garrick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.100
as well as the first human Green Lantern,&nbsp;
Alan Scott. However, "Black Adam" will focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.900
on other JSA members including Hawkman,&nbsp;
Dr. Fate, Atom Smasher, and Cyclone.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:57.660
How these heroes came to be in the DCEU is&nbsp;
unknown. Unlike Superman or Wonder Woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.940
we haven't received an origin tale for any of&nbsp;
these heroes. However, if they're anything like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.920
their comic book counterparts, Dr. Fate and&nbsp;
Hawkman are both born from ancient powers. Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:13.260
Fate is a creation of a cosmic deity while&nbsp;
Hawkman was the Egyptian prince Khufu who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:17.400
after being killed with a mystical&nbsp;
dagger, is bound to be reincarnated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.920
upon death. During the JSA era, Hawkman&nbsp;
is reborn as Carter Hall who adopts the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:28.380
mantle of Hawkman using alien antigravity&nbsp;
Nth metal to power his armor and weaponry.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:34.200
As for Atom Smasher, he's the heroic grandson of&nbsp;
the supervillain Cyclotron in the comics, gifted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:39.180
with super strength and the ability to control&nbsp;
the size and density of his body. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:44.400
Cyclone is the granddaughter of the original&nbsp;
Red Tornado and possesses the powers of flight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:51.180
wind control, and sound wave control. Both&nbsp;
are legacy heroes with strong ties to the JSA.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.920
"Black Adam" occurs primarily in the&nbsp;
modern day after the events of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:01.620
theatrical-released "Justice League." This&nbsp;
means the JSA and Justice League co-exist in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:06.540
the same era. However, this doesn't explain&nbsp;
why the JSA are the only heroes who seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:11.040
to be responding to the climactic events&nbsp;
after Black Adam emerges from his prison.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.620
While the Justice League took&nbsp;
some time to come together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:19.920
its individual members have been active for&nbsp;
years. Kal-El revealed himself years ago as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:24.120
Superman while Black Adam was still stuck&nbsp;
in limbo. Wonder Woman made herself known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:29.400
to humanity during the First World War. Bruce&nbsp;
Wayne has been operating as Batman for decades.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:35.340
And both Aquaman and the Flash had superhero&nbsp;
careers long before joining the Justice League.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:41.640
The greater DCEU is familiar with these rock&nbsp;
stars, but the JSA still seems relatively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:45.780
unknown. It'll be interesting to see how&nbsp;
the timelines link up and learn what the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:49.200
Justice League is doing when Black&nbsp;
Adam makes himself known. Notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:54.780
Amanda Waller from DCEU's "Suicide Squad"&nbsp;
films is working with the JSA and has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.780 --> 00:07:00.090
some pull with certain League members,&nbsp;
including a certain famous Kryptonian.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:05.100
Empowered by the gods themselves, Black&nbsp;
Adam is an insanely powerful being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:10.320
and what better way to show this by having&nbsp;
him challenge the alpha of DC superheroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:16.200
Superman? In DC Comics, Black Adam has always&nbsp;
been a formidable foe for powerhouses like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:21.480
Superman and Shazam. Notably, aside from&nbsp;
Kryptonite, Superman is vulnerable to magic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:26.280
something Black Adam can produce punishing&nbsp;
amounts of thanks to his divine gifts.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:31.860
After a Twitter fan expressed a desire to see&nbsp;
these two titans come together. Johnson retweeted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:38.040
the message and shared that he always aims to&nbsp;
listen to his audience. "I hear you &amp; I always got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:43.440
you," stated the Rock. In the film's mid credit&nbsp;
scene, we see Johnson make good on his promise.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:48.060
After being informed by Amanda Waller&nbsp;
that he is not to leave Khandaq's borders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:54.180
Black Adam arrogantly informs her that no one can&nbsp;
stop him from doing what he wants. In response,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:59.520
Waller sends Superman to confront Black Adam,&nbsp;
who informs the demigod that they should talk.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:04.320
No word on whether or not this will lead to a&nbsp;
big screen battle between the two, but with Henry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:09.780
Cavill back in the Superman suit, we'll likely&nbsp;
be seeing more of both the hero and anti-hero.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:15.300
Shazam and Black Adam are like the Joker and&nbsp;
Batman. Young Billy Batson as the all-powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.760
hero Shazam seeks to do good and uphold a&nbsp;
heroic standard. Black Adam doesn't live by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:26.820
a code of any kind. His goal is singular&nbsp;
in his mind, and no act is too amoral or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:31.140
dicey if it furthers his objective of&nbsp;
obliterating tyranny and opposition.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:36.120
Yet despite these moral differences,&nbsp;
Shazam and Black Adam are ultimately two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:41.220
sides of the same coin, imbued with godly&nbsp;
powers by the same wizard. In the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:45.180
the wizard saw the error of his ways and&nbsp;
banished Black Adam until a hero could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:49.800
be called forward to defeat him. With the rise&nbsp;
of Billy Batson as Shazam, that time had come.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:55.440
However, this is a film focused on the "bad&nbsp;
guy" — a move meant to position Black Adam as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:00.960
a sympathetic anti-hero. Shazam is nowhere to&nbsp;
be seen, and director Jaume Collet-Serra said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:05.640
not to expect a Shazam-Black Adam match-up just&nbsp;
yet. In an interview with "Variety," he stated:

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.300
"Our movie is an original story.&nbsp;
By the time the movie ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.240
he doesn't know who Shazam or Superman is."

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.800
However, it's fairly certain that "Black Adam"&nbsp;
takes place after the first "Shazam!" film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:21.960
If Black Adam were around during the events of&nbsp;
"Shazam!" he would have most certainly confronted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:26.700
Billy over his powers. Black Adam doesn't want&nbsp;
a champion standing in the way of his goals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:33.360
and wants to be a supreme power. Eliminating&nbsp;
Shazam is the only means to that end. The two will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:39.616
inevitably meet in the DCEU, however, even if it&nbsp;
isn't in Black Adam's first outing. It's destiny.

00:09:39.616 --> 00:09:44.220
While Shazam won't appear in "Black Adam,"&nbsp;
audiences will be seeing Billy Batson's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:50.220
superpowered alter ego very soon. "Shazam: Fury&nbsp;
of the Gods'' is set to release in March 2023.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:57.720
Instead of Black Adam, however, the sequel&nbsp;
will feature a wildly new antagonist in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:02.400
form of Helen Mirren's Hespera, a jealous&nbsp;
god seeking the power of Shazam for herself.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.780
With Black Adam busy contending with&nbsp;
Intergang in Kahndaq and Shazam working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:10.380
with his family to dispel evil on the&nbsp;
other side of the world in Philly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:15.000
it's unlikely that these two will come to&nbsp;
blows. It also remains to be seen if either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:20.100
film will tease a future clash or if either&nbsp;
character cameos in the opposite film. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:24.720
a timeline perspective, however, consider&nbsp;
these films either happening concurrently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:30.000
or relatively close together, allowing the&nbsp;
two champions to remain separate… for now.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:35.520
With the future of the Justice League up in&nbsp;
the air, there may be a brand-new world for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:41.040
Black Adam to conquer in the DCEU. Ben Affleck is&nbsp;
wrapping up his time as Batman with the upcoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:45.360
"The Flash" movie. It's hard to believe Ray&nbsp;
Fisher will be back as Cyborg any time soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:49.920
after his feud with Warner Bros. And the&nbsp;
Flash, as portrayed by Ezra Miller, will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:55.080
almost definitely not return outside of his solo&nbsp;
project, after the actor's various alleged crimes.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:59.880
Meanwhile, Wonder Woman is primed for a third&nbsp;
film, rounding out a trilogy for the Amazonian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:04.320
warrior. "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;
is also in the works, while Henry Cavill's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:09.360
involvement as Superman in future DCEU movies&nbsp;
has been confirmed with that post credit scene.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:14.760
With Black Adam about to make his mark in the&nbsp;
DCEU, could Johnson's take on the Man in Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:20.760
be the one that leads us into the future of DCEU?&nbsp;
The remaining heroes — Aquaman, Wonder Woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:26.280
Shazam, and whoever from the JSA survives&nbsp;
"Black Adam" — could use a central hero or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:31.500
a unifying villain. The film universe is on the&nbsp;
precipice of a shake-up as Warner Bros. seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:37.320
bent on abandoning what Zack Snyder began. With&nbsp;
a leading man like Johnson, anything is possible.

